==Finnish==

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|fi|gmq-osw|tisdagher}}, from {{der|fi|gmw-pro|*Tīwas dag}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{fi-pronunciation|a=Fi-tiistai.ogg}}

===Noun===
{{enum|fi|maanantai|keskiviikko|day of the week|ti}}
{{head|fi|noun}}

# [[Tuesday]] {{gloss|day of the week; the second day of the week in Finland and in the ISO 8601 standard}}

====Usage notes====
As with all days of the week in Finnish, the essive case ({{m|fi||tiistaina}}) is usually used when talking about what will happen or happened on a Tuesday.

